Package: dispctrl-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: DispCtrl <https://github.com/jesvijonathan/DispCtrl/issues>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libx11-6, libxrandr2, libxi6, libxfixes3, libxcomposite1, libcairo2, libpango-1.0-0, libpangocairo-1.0-0, libfontconfig1, libice6, libsm6
Recommends: ddcutil, x11-xserver-utils
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/jesvijonathan/DispCtrl
Description: per-monitor brightness, dimming and night light
 DispCtrl for Linux sets each display's brightness - external monitors over
 DDC/CI (through ddcutil) and a laptop's own panel through its backlight -
 and warms or dims any display through its gamma ramp, with a night light
 schedule kept by a small user service. A command line (dispctrl-linux) and
 a window (dispctrl-linux-gui). Night light and dimming need an X11 session.
